WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.181
Lest We Forget.

00:00:01.181 --> 00:00:03.556
How Canada Betrayed Its Veterans.

00:00:03.556 --> 00:00:06.613
They were promised a country worthy of their sacrifice.

00:00:06.613 --> 00:00:11.284
They were given a backlog, a budget cut, and a brochure for medical assistance in dying.

00:00:11.284 --> 00:00:12.318
Section 1.

00:00:12.318 --> 00:00:14.443
Veterans Affairs By the Numbers.

00:00:14.443 --> 00:00:17.022
A department failing the people it exists to serve.

00:00:17.022 --> 00:00:24.999
Over 11,000 veterans wait in the disability claims backlog while the department inexplicably lapses hundreds of millions in unspent funding.

00:00:24.999 --> 00:00:26.181
Section 2.

00:00:26.181 --> 00:00:28.579
The Medical Assistance in Dying Question.

00:00:28.579 --> 00:00:35.363
Veterans who called seeking assistance for injuries sustained in service were systematically offered state-sponsored euthanasia.

00:00:35.363 --> 00:00:39.443
No veteran should ever be offered death when they are asking for help to live.

00:00:39.443 --> 00:00:40.579
Section 3.

00:00:40.579 --> 00:00:41.863
The Funding Gap.

00:00:41.863 --> 00:00:48.477
Between 2018 and 2023, the government lapsed over 3 billion dollars in approved veterans funding.

00:00:48.477 --> 00:00:53.261
Money was budgeted, but Veterans Affairs simply failed to spend it on the people it was meant for.

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:54.409
Section 4.

00:00:54.409 --> 00:00:56.534
Phoenix Pay and Veterans.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:57.749
Broken Twice.

00:00:57.749 --> 00:01:08.011
The 2.2 billion dollar Phoenix Pay failure devastated veterans transitioning to federal employment, leaving many without paychecks while simultaneously navigating the disability backlog.

00:01:08.011 --> 00:01:09.284
Section 5.

00:01:09.284 --> 00:01:10.795
The Office Closures.

00:01:10.795 --> 00:01:16.602
In 2014, the Harper government closed 9 Veterans Affairs district offices across Canada.

00:01:16.602 --> 00:01:21.306
Veterans in rural and remote communities lost face-to-face access to caseworkers.

00:01:21.306 --> 00:01:24.340
Some had to travel hundreds of kilometres for appointments.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:26.249
Many simply stopped seeking help.

00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:27.499
Section 6.

00:01:27.499 --> 00:01:29.363
Operational Stress Injuries.

00:01:29.363 --> 00:01:30.761
The invisible wounds.

00:01:30.761 --> 00:01:37.659
Post-traumatic stress disorder, depression, anxiety, and moral injury affect tens of thousands of Canadian veterans.

00:01:37.659 --> 00:01:42.477
Wait times for mental health services at Veterans Affairs routinely exceed 6 months.

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:46.829
The veteran suicide rate remains significantly higher than the general population.

00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:48.102
Section 7.

00:01:48.102 --> 00:01:50.170
The Record of Broken Promises.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:56.613
Decade after decade, Canadian governments have promised veterans better care, faster processing, more support.

00:01:56.613 --> 00:02:00.329
And decade after decade, those promises have been broken.

00:02:00.329 --> 00:02:03.193
The Veterans Charter was supposed to fix everything.

00:02:03.193 --> 00:02:04.079
It didn't.

00:02:04.079 --> 00:02:07.238
The New Veterans Charter was supposed to modernize everything.

00:02:07.238 --> 00:02:08.977
It created new problems.

00:02:08.977 --> 00:02:09.999
Section 8.

00:02:09.999 --> 00:02:11.670
Source Attribution.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:25.068
Every number, every claim, every fact on this page comes from the public record: Auditor General reports, Parliamentary Budget Officer analyses, Veterans Affairs annual reports, House of Commons committee testimony, and court documents.

00:02:25.068 --> 00:02:27.488
Nothing is alleged without attribution.

00:02:27.488 --> 00:02:28.374
Section.

00:02:28.374 --> 00:02:33.181
The Military Pipeline — DND Departmental Plan 2025-26.

00:02:33.181 --> 00:02:37.261
The same institution that fails veterans also fails serving members.

00:02:37.261 --> 00:02:55.579
The DND Departmental Plan 2025-26, tabled in Parliament, reveals that 72.9 percent of military occupations have critical shortfalls, only 30.4 percent of members feel the CAF provides a reasonable quality of life, and 22 percent self-identify as victims of harassment.

00:02:55.579 --> 00:03:01.624
These are the people who will become veterans — already broken by the institution before VAC gets to break them again.

00:03:01.624 --> 00:03:02.795
Lest We Forget.

00:03:02.795 --> 00:03:06.103
Those words are carved into cenotaphs across this country.

00:03:06.103 --> 00:03:07.556
But we have forgotten.

00:03:07.556 --> 00:03:09.840
We forgot when we closed their offices.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.670
We forgot when we let billions lapse unspent.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:15.261
We forgot when we offered them death instead of help.

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:19.488
Every veteran who served this country was promised that Canada would take care of them.

00:03:19.488 --> 00:03:21.272
Canada broke that promise.

00:03:21.272 --> 00:03:22.795
The law that applies.

00:03:22.795 --> 00:03:26.011
The Rome Statute criminalises crimes against humanity.

00:03:26.011 --> 00:03:28.636
Canada was the first country to implement it.

00:03:28.636 --> 00:03:35.954
When a veteran calls asking for help and is offered death instead, that violates the Nuremberg Code — consent without coercion.

00:03:35.954 --> 00:03:40.886
And Canada abolished the death penalty for convicted murderers in 1976.

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:44.284
Then legalised it for the men and women who defended this country.

00:03:44.284 --> 00:03:46.113
The kill economics.

00:03:46.113 --> 00:03:49.136
MAID costs 8,150 dollars.

00:03:49.136 --> 00:03:52.863
Palliative care costs 28,835.

00:03:52.863 --> 00:03:59.181
The government saves 20,685 dollars every time a veteran dies instead of receiving care.

00:03:59.181 --> 00:04:03.102
102 doctors killed 373 people each.

00:04:03.102 --> 00:04:07.488
428 legal violations — zero referred to police.

00:04:07.488 --> 00:04:12.340
Kiano Vafaeian, age 26, was coached into death by his doctor.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:15.170
Kelsi Sheren testified that 20 veterans

00:04:15.218 --> 00:04:18.554
have documented proof of being offered MAID when seeking healthcare.

00:04:18.554 --> 00:04:20.111
The government saves money.

00:04:20.111 --> 00:04:22.077
The veterans lose their lives.

00:04:22.077 --> 00:04:24.156
The PM profits through Brookfield.
